kosha metal

  -- generic metal node. the common-sense entry point for metallic materials.
  -- bridges to: metals-varga (chemistry) + solid (thermodynamics) + pbr (3d).
  -- specific metals: iron, copper, aluminium, gold, silver — each has own node.
  -- alloys (steel, brass, bronze) are in composites.
  --
  -- everyday properties:
  --   solid at room temperature (except mercury Hg)
  --   shiny (lustrous) — free electrons reflect photons
  --   conducts electricity and heat
  --   malleable and ductile — can be shaped, drawn
  --   relatively high density (except aluminium, lithium)
  --   coefficient of restitution: varies by metal (steel ~0.65, aluminium ~0.5)

  "common-sense-varga-vishesa"
  "materials-varga-vishesa"
  "metals-varga-vishesa"

  "solid-sthita"
  "conductor-swarupa lustrous-swarupa malleable-swarupa"
  "coefficient-of-restitution-yukta"
  "domain-3d-yukta pbr-yukta"

